      en: "Teahupoo Coast on Tahiti's southeast side is known for one of the heaviest waves in surfing. The wave breaks over a shallow coral reef, with depths of 0.5 m at low tide. Wave heights can exceed 7 m (23 ft). The site hosts the annual Billabong Pro Tahiti surfing competition. The reef extends 200 m offshore. The village of Teahupoo has a population of 1,500. The wave was first surfed in the 1980s.",
